   "subject": "Clustering for EFA",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi everyone,<div><br></div><div>I am analysing a dataset where participants are clustered by families. Accounting for clustering by family is necessary according to ICC calculations. There are no other multilevel effects.</div><div><br></div><div>Can anyone please advise whether it is possible, either via lavaan or another R package, to account for this clustering for an EFA analysis?</div><div><br></div><div>I am familiar with this option on Mplus but I am new to R. The rest of the syntax that I&#39;m using is all on R, and multiple EFAs need to be run, which is why I&#39;m keen to see if I can keep all analyses within R. </div><div><br></div><div>Thank you in advance for your help.</div><div><br></div><div>Kind regards,</div><div>Tracey</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "euSihI4EAQAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2024-06-11T10:36:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: Clustering for EFA",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Accounting for clustering by family is necessary according to ICC calculations. There are no other multilevel effects.</div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div>If you are not interested in modeling Level-2 covariance structure, then you can just pass the clustering variable to lavaan(cluster=) with a single-level model.  You will get cluster-robust <i>SE</i>s and tests.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;font-size:16px\"><div><p style=\"margin:0cm;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\">Terrence D. Jorgensen </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\">   (he, him, his)</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\"><br>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics<br>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<br><a href=\"https://eur04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Furldefense.com%2Fv3%2F__http%3A%2Fwww.uva.nl%2Fprofile%2Ft.d.jorgensen__%3B!!D9dNQwwGXtA!RdmdUd4WPRh7g7WAPQViCxUMWWjfCFpYPBs_GolbBQ-8m6MZFr9q93hgVEl4SnZ0IqPtX17qKMdVIrknwgORIVJK-9w%24&amp;data=05%...%40uva.nl%7C787cddbcbb304d36cd2808dc896574a6%7Ca0f1cacd618c4403b94576fb3d6874e5%7C0%7C0%7C638536316050859803%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=m0lXbiRM61LU8SlXmHCEAbZGCI%2F39ZSVK%2FOV6SuCMpY%3D&amp;reserved=0\" title=\"https://eur04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Furldefense.com%2Fv3%2F__http%3A%2Fwww.uva.nl%2Fprofile%2Ft.d.jorgensen__%3B!!D9dNQwwGXtA!RdmdUd4WPRh7g7WAPQViCxUMWWjfCFpYPBs_GolbBQ-8m6MZFr9q93hgVEl4SnZ0IqPtX17qKMdVIrknwgORIVJK-9w%24&amp;data=05%...%40uva.nl%7C787cddbcbb304d36cd2808dc896574a6%7Ca0f1cacd618c4403b94576fb3d6874e5%7C0%7C0%7C638536316050859803%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=m0lXbiRM61LU8SlXmHCEAbZGCI%2F39ZSVK%2FOV6SuCMpY%3D&amp;reserved=0\" style=\"color:rgb(0,120,215);text-decoration-line:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-safer